      "text": [
        " «إِنْ كَانَ أَغْلَقَ اَلْبَابَ عَلَيْهِ بَعْدَ مَا أَحْرَمَ فَعَلَيْهِ دَمٌ وَ إِنْ كَانَ أَغْلَقَهُ قَبْلَ أَنْ يُحْرِمَ وَ هُوَ حَلاَلٌ فَعَلَيْهِ ثَمَنُهُ»."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.2351 - Sulayman ibn Khalid asked Abu Abdullah (as) about a man who closed his door on a bird, causing it to die.\nImam (as) replied: \"If he closed the door on it after entering the state of ihram, then he must offer a sacrificial animal (damm). If he closed it before entering ihram while he was in a permissible state, he must pay its value.\""
        ]
      }
